.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="The harmonic bond potential (~chemistrykit.md.systems.pair_potentials.HarmonicBond) is the small-oscillation limit of the anharmonic Morse potential -- they agree near the equilibrium separation but diverge away from it (Morse correctly flattens out toward a finite dissociation energy; harmonic does not). DiatomicOscillator integrates the classical two-body bond-vibration problem via the shared velocity-Verlet integrator, for either potential.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/md/pair_potentials/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_morse_vs_harmonic_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/md/pair_potentials/plot_01_morse_vs_harmonic`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Morse vs. harmonic bond potentials, and diatomic bond vibration</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/md/pair_potentials/plot_01_morse_vs_harmonic`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="The Buckingham (exp-6) potential replaces the Lennard-Jones r^{-12} repulsive wall with an exponential -- closer to the true quantum-mechanical electron-overlap repulsion -- while keeping the same r^{-6} dispersion attraction. Matched to a Lennard-Jones potential&#x27;s well depth, position, and long-range tail, the two agree closely everywhere near and beyond the minimum. But the exponential repulsion is eventually overwhelmed by the unbounded -C/r^6 attractive term at short enough range, so the Buckingham potential has a second, spurious turnover well inside the true minimum: past that point it falls back toward -\infty as r\to0 instead of diverging to +\infty the way Lennard-Jones&#x27;s pure r^{-12} repulsion does.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/md/pair_potentials/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_03_buckingham_vs_lj_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/md/pair_potentials/plot_03_buckingham_vs_lj`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Buckingham vs. Lennard-Jones: exponential repulsion and its inner turnover</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/md/pair_potentials/plot_03_buckingham_vs_lj`

